From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebCore: cairo out (USE_CAIRO off), the engine's own pictures and paths

Cairo-out item 7 (docs/CAIRO-OUT-0083.md). USE_CAIRO is off and
USE_AMIGA_GRAPHICS on: cairo, pixman and libpng are no longer built into
the engine. What cairo gave WebCore is the engine's own:

- AmigaImage: premultiplied ARGB32 words (A, R, G, B in memory on the
  68k), its own or someone else's held until the last reference goes.
  PlatformImagePtr is RefPtr<AmigaImage>; NativeImageAmiga.cpp.
- ImageBufferAmigaBackend: an AmigaImage drawn into by a
  GraphicsContextOpenGPU (canvas, filters, layers); pixel copies through
  BGRA8 rows on a big-endian CPU.
- PathAmiga: WebCore's PathStream inside, with hit testing (fill by
  winding on the path flattened to lines, stroke by distance) and stroke
  bounds.
- GraphicsAmiga.cpp: Gradient::fill, Pattern's platform pattern (none),
  a decoder frame as a picture, PNG out through the datatypes.
- ShareableBitmapAmiga.cpp, FontOpenFont.cpp (outlines, bounds and
  advances from gfopenfont), FontCascadeAmigaInlines.h.
- gfopenfont faces without the cairo user font: OpenFontFace owns its
  OFFace; advances are the font's hmtx at the size rounded to whole
  pixels, as cairo's metrics hinting gave them; glyph outlines as Paths.
- GraphicsContextOpenGPU keeps the state cairo kept (the transform, the
  clip's bounds, caps, joins, miter limit, dashes) and draws everything
  through OpenGPU. Transparency layers are pictures of their own put on
  what is under them by opacity and operator. Glyph runs OpenFont can't
  draw with OF_DrawGlyphsA are their outlines filled as paths; spelling
  markers a zigzag; focus rings strokes. Not drawn here yet (counted):
  blend modes other than normal (drawn normal), shadows under a scale or
  turn, clipToImageBuffer's mask (its rectangle clips), picture
  orientations.
- PNG stays the one encoding (MIMETypeRegistry). It is written by
  gfopenpng.datatype first: the list of PNG writers still named it
  openpng, so png.datatype wrote the page remapped to 4 pens.

